{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:3b8e738940cd51c1","name":"A-7 Hunter Interceptor","source":{"id":"source:reference-3b8e738940cd51c1","title":"A-7 Hunter Interceptor","revision":15590,"timestamp":"2024-08-18T00:52:50Z","sha256":"7a87c1a8c58e315a74407b9a57ded318595aba3b2b568a4d2c0ec2602183e2d1","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=15590","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=A-7%20Hunter%20Interceptor&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-3b8e738940cd51c1","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Unleashed Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Unleashed_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Empire","referenceId":"reference:f9c9a48674cc3415"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The rapidly growing military needs of the New Order created opportunities for companies to build new shipyards, especially if they could interest the Empire in a new line of vessels to be the standard of Imperial fleets. Kuat Drive Yards earned vast profits building Imperial ",{"tag":"a","children":["Star Destroyers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Star_Destroyers"}," and wanted to provide the Empire with its ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"}," fleets as well. The main entrant for this role was the A-7 Hunter Interceptor, an update of a long-successful line of cheap, simple, fast ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighters","referenceId":"reference:e127af2636e147fc"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["For the first few years after ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"},", many Imperial officers assumed that the A-7 Hunter Interceptor would become the new standard snub fighter of the Empire and bought dozens of the fighters to outfit their ship's hangars. When the ",{"tag":"a","children":["TIE Fighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/TIE_Fighter","referenceId":"reference:726e84ae35ac767c"}," was instead selected, the A-7 waned in popularity among Imperials, though it could still be found on ships in fringe systems. Many of the fighters eventually ended up being used by mercenaries and insurgents.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The A-7 is similar to a TIE in many respects. It has no ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hyperdrive"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hyperdrive","referenceId":"reference:6774bf610b6e6f09"}," or shields, only two ",{"tag":"a","children":["Laser Cannons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Laser_Cannons"},", and few support systems. Though not as fast or maneuverable as later designs such as ",{"tag":"a","children":["TIE Interceptors"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/TIE_Interceptors"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["A-Wings"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/A-Wings"},", it is more agile than a typical TIE. Ultimately, it's likely that its higher construction cost led to the Empire passing it over.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Skilled)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["A-7 Hunter Interceptor Statistics (CL 6)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Huge ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +8; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +6\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.